From 8643ff13af9c901cf57a695892e801cc540bcd6a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:56:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PUBLISH-FIX-108: a 5-second stall with its own stack trace -
 tail reads

Production, deployment eb532bba, 03:41:

  MAIN THREAD STALLED 5s: running JavaScript (CPU-bound on the main thread)
  MAIN THREAD STACK (paused): canonicalDigest learning/contracts.js:53:39
                              <- patternRecordError learning/contracts.js:2...
  CPU LOAD 60s: busy 58784ms idle 1845ms (event-loop utilization 97%)

The learning store caches each journal keyed on the file's SIZE. Any
growth the cache did not itself make - the bucket restore, the gate
study's child process, a sweep that appended more than the cache saw -
threw the WHOLE cache away and re-read and re-VALIDATED every record
from byte zero. patternRecordError alone recomputes two SHA-256
canonical digests per record, and these journals hold tens of thousands
of records. Against a 500 ms receipt-to-decision limit and a 10 s
proposal law, that stall can eat a bite outright.

These journals are append-only, so growth means new lines at the end.
cachedRows now reads and validates only the TAIL and extends the cache.
Every new record is validated exactly as before - nothing is trusted
unread; only the re-validation of records already read is gone. The
derived indexes are dropped so they rebuild lazily without any crypto.
Anything that is not clean append-only growth - a shrink, an offset
that is not a line boundary, a torn final line - falls back to the full
re-read it always did. Tail reads and full re-reads are both counted.

This is the same class PUBLISH-FIX-45 fixed for appendOutcome and
PUBLISH-FIX-83 item 24 fixed for patterns; the remaining hole was
growth by another writer.

Fenced by test/publish-fix-108-tail-read.test.js (5), whose fixture is
asserted to be accepted so the drill cannot silently skip its own
mechanism: external append == full re-read row for row, a torn line is
never half a record, a shrink falls back, and the journals are still
append-only with nothing deleted.

